## What Problem This Solves

Native-owned model resolution discards a larger context window when the exact native catalog row carries a finite, provider-reported value.

## Why This Change Was Made

The shared resolver now carries that matching row's positive, finite, non-synthetic context window into runtime metadata. Unknown or synthetic capacity keeps the conservative 200,000-token fallback.

The Muse provider's current `model/list` output has no context window. This PR does not claim to fix Muse's effective serving window or history-transfer sizing, and it does not use Meta API catalog capacity as Muse runtime capacity.

### Scope

This PR covers the shared resolver contract only. Related: #195300 (this PR does not close the Muse issue).

## User Impact

Native harnesses can size retained history using a genuine provider-reported catalog window when their catalog owner supplies one. Unknown capacity keeps the 200,000-token fallback.

## Evidence

- Focused regression at head `19d8e75ad93cf5ca59eafcb6f58a786883b9783f`: `pnpm test src/agents/defaults.test.ts --maxWorkers=1` — 2 tests passed; 1.44s local wall time. Exact-head CI shard also passed both tests; Vitest duration was 127ms and the shard reported 1.69s.
- Production resolver proof used the same synthetic catalog row on validation base `c74999244a71333ad02074c307c5b1bed69579aa` and PR head `19d8e75ad93cf5ca59eafcb6f58a786883b9783f`:

