## What Problem This Solves

Large agent fleets can delay Gateway agent admission when usage refreshes start across many agents at once.

Fixes #195270

## Why This Change Was Made

A process-wide FIFO permit pool bounds independent refresh queues before they reach shared worker lanes. Extracting the admission logic keeps the runtime file under its 700-line cap. A report waiting on its selected session can wake the queue and bypass the fleet permit once.

The new tracked allocation covers 128 regression-test lines for cross-agent fairness and selected-session priority. The shared test-line baseline stays unchanged.

## User Impact

Gateways can continue admitting agent turns while usage caches catch up, and a requested session read keeps priority over unrelated refresh work.

