Closes #168147. Related:#168109(closed,unmerged).

## What Problem This Solves

Supported environment templates with nonempty credential fallbacks can appear unredacted in authenticated configuration snapshots, including when the environment supplies a different active value. The shared owner also serves configuration previews and /config show.

## Why This Change Was Made

Use the canonical environment-template parser to exempt only a whole, secret-free reference. Nonempty fallbacks are credential material. Current main already compares parsed raw output with the independently redacted structured view; once the predicate is correct, that existing guard safely withholds escaped/different authored fallback text. The earlier extra collection and raw branch are removed. SecretRefs remain the recommended alternative but do not repair existing supported configurations; no new library, plugin or redaction subsystem is needed.

## User Impact

Fallback material is absent from public config projections. Bare and empty-fallback references, blank values and nonsensitive fallbacks remain editable. Sentinel writes retain authored environment bindings; config.patch readback checks the disk result. Raw text can be withheld through the existing raw:null/structured-editor contract, so source formatting/comments are not returned in that view. No config/default, protocol, permission, schema, migration or dependency change.

Security review and intentional-fixture qualification remain maintainer gates.

