## What Problem This Solves

When a Gateway deadline stops a run with buffered assistant text, a later model request can lose that unfinished text. A successor can also read history while the timeout report is pending. Merged #142135 supplies the deadline terminal report and CLI persistence context; this PR addresses the remaining buffered-output and admission gaps.

## Why This Change Was Made

Capture the buffer before abort cleanup and pass it through the existing terminal lifecycle owner. The existing SQLite report transaction stores the timeout statement and JSON-quoted unfinished output in one `run-failed-before-reply` custom message. Existing readers understand that record format. This PR adds no table, index, required field, schema version, replay exception, or backfill.

Wait for the same agent/session's timeout persistence before and after work admission. The second check covers a deadline observed while admission waits. Both waits run outside the session writer, allowing the terminal write to acquire it. If the observed write rejects, the pending successor receives the error before dispatch and releases its reservation, abort controller, and admission lease.

## User Impact

The report states that a timed-out turn may have performed work; it makes no claim of completion, external success, or rollback. Existing assistant rows are retained. A partial assistant row does not suppress the timeout report. Normal completion, user cancellation, and ordinary failures retain their existing behavior. Transactional authority validation and per-run deduplication remain with the existing owner.

