The wrappers retain per-phase stdout/stderr, exit status, timing, SQLite manifests and results. Session activity is current to avoid replacing the seed through idle reset; historical message timestamps and payload bytes remain fixed and are checked. Seed state is synthetic; no existing user database or credentials are required.

