## What Problem This Solves

Fixes: PowerShell tab completion returns no matches when the cursor is inside an argument and text after the cursor does not match the desired completion. For example, `--shell f|xsh` should offer `fish` (`|` marks the cursor).

## User Impact

Users can complete command names, option names, and option values while editing the middle of a command, including quoted values and short option groups.

## Why This Change Was Made

PowerShell supplies the entire current word and AST, including the suffix after the cursor. Normalize that element to its cursor prefix before the existing completion logic runs. PowerShell's parser handles partial quotes without evaluating them. Preserve whether a current token exists even when its decoded prefix is empty.

## Evidence

- Generated the script through `pnpm --silent openclaw completion --shell powershell` from clean builds of base `3d6914aaad58c3f02ad23c6e4677801a6f100f4c` and head `9f156b31c1246b04416d658b057459a3dec444b0`. Ran native `CommandCompletion.CompleteInput` with explicit cursor positions on Windows, Node 24.22.1 and PowerShell 7.6.5, using isolated temporary configuration and state. Five mid-token cases failed on base and pass on head; three control cases pass on both.
- `pnpm test src/cli/completion-cli.test.ts --maxWorkers=1`: base with the regression table had 7 failures; fixed source has 35 passed, 18 platform-dependent skips, and 0 failures. Measured command wall time: 7.83 s; test execution: 3.34 s. CI seconds: pending the upstream run.
- Related alias, visibility, and configured-plugin option-shadowing tests: 9 passed, 13 skipped, 0 failures.
- Targeted source/test typechecks, lint, format, test-line budget, and `git diff --check` passed. Both normal runtime builds passed. No live services or personal shell profile were used.
- The existing native cursor test is extended in place; seven distinct regression boundaries add 8 net test lines, recorded in a per-change allocation. The native shell boundary is necessary because the defect depends on PowerShell's actual word/AST/cursor contract. Production changes are net +12 lines, with no new helper or dependency.

